# Rules for Cloudflare Pages, copied to out/_redirects by the build.
# Syntax: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Search Console reads its verification file at this exact address and does
# not follow redirects. Pages normally redirects /name.html to /name, so this
# rule serves the file in place with a 200.
/google3419091e9a1248e3.html /google3419091e9a1248e3 200

# The site used to show a photo here. Pages keeps files from earlier deploys
# at their old address for up to a week, and redirects run before that, so
# this rule makes sure the old photo is never served again.
/me.jpg /mascot-avatar.png 301

# Removed blog posts. Old links go to the blog page instead of an error,
# and Pages can't serve a copy left over from an earlier deploy.
/blog/how-this-site-is-built /blog/ 301
/blog/nextjs-docker-oracle-cloud /blog/ 301
/blog/how-this-site-is-built/* /blog/ 301
/blog/nextjs-docker-oracle-cloud/* /blog/ 301
